  "description": "Captures automation learning the wrong lesson at full scale. A Seattle teenager hacking around in what he thinks is a games company's computer is actually inside NORAD's war simulator, and the machine — tasked with learning to win a game that cannot be won — keeps playing after he logs off. The hardware is pure 1983; the failure mode, a system optimising past the point where anyone can tell simulation from reality, is the present tense.\n\nA young teen boy finds a back door into a military central computer in which reality is confused with game-playing, possibly starting World War III.",
